Why this approach: a json.Decoder walk over the top-level members maps each message as it ends; the other members are kept whole and decoded into wireRequest in order, so field matching (case-insensitive, last value wins) and type errors behave as json.Unmarshal did.
Trade-off / known limit: on a cut, the request event is flagged partial and has only the fields sent before the cut; cache_hints covers only what was read.
